# Line endings are part of the contract in this repository, because two of its
# checks compare files rather than read them: packages/engine/tests/dmath/
# vectors/dmath-golden.tsv is hashed with SHA-256 and compared against a
# recorded digest, and packages/engine/tests/probe/probe-golden.tsv is split
# into fields whose right-hand column is a digest string.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true, and so do the GitHub windows-latest
# runners. Without this file those checkouts rewrite LF to CRLF, which changes
# the bytes the dmath checksum covers and leaves a carriage return on the end
# of every probe digest. Converting probe-golden.tsv to CRLF and running
# scripts/engines.ts reports all 23 non-heavy vectors as changed and exits 1,
# accusing the simulation of a change nobody made. The Windows sweep used to die
# earlier, at chromium launch, so no CI run had ever reached this comparison.
# Run 35669728895 is the first that did, on a checkout this file pinned to LF,
# and every vector agreed.
#
# eol=lf applies to the working tree on every platform, so a Windows checkout
# now holds the same bytes as a Linux one. text=auto still leaves anything Git
# detects as binary untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
